# Chance — Barclay's lantern spirit

**First played appearance in [Delvers S3E09 — I Am The Natural One](../../episodes/S3E09.md)** with guest tortle cleric/cartographer [Barclay Vandergeist/Bendergeist](../characters/barclay-vandergeist.md). **Chance** is the short name the guest attributes to **a sentient force or spirit within a lamp/lantern that sheds a ghostly blue light**, allegedly found on an earlier expedition. **No written D&D race/class, spell/item stat block, exact spirit identity, age, alignment, named previous owner or confirmed life/death history** is established. GM tells Krandal on a **Religion 13** check that it is **“likely an undead spirit”**, not species/provenance proof. Initially Barclay says it gained powers and began forming a spectral hand capable of physically shaking other people and writing rough marks in dirt (poorly writes **“hi”**); it doesn't audibly speak sentences in this episode. Barclay understands its own name “Chance” from dirt writing, admits it might be a misspelling.

**Physical/appearance continuity for art:** One **carried lantern** with **blue/ghostly glow**, capable of projecting **one spectral hand**, not a full independent human body, monster, glowing human head, genie or explicit face. Lantern silhouette/material, panels/ornaments and hand colour other than ghostly not described. It stays with Barclay while travelling from his **mushroom camp** through paired pressure plates, stone golems, grick wind chamber, forest exit, Veggie Sticks and Atomer tree arrival; **no proven transfer of lantern to core Delvers or extinction**.

**Production spoiler caution:** Kyle ends S3E09 remarking that listeners who have followed the show may recognize the name “Chance,” explicitly **declines to explain identity** and suggests checking the wiki. **This is a hint only**, not a confirmed diegetic revelation, and no links across *The Wastes*, *Inverse*, or earlier Delvers NPCs should be forged without direct independently sourced evidence.

